You can also install the useful network tools available in Bullseye:

sudo apt install -y \
nmap \
tcpdump \
wireshark \
arp-scan \
net-tools \
netdiscover \
aircrack-ng \
iw \
macchanger \
john \
hydra


Start with sudo arp-scan --localnet, then use Nmap on an individual device to inspect its open ports:
sudo nmap -sV 192.168.1.8

Scan all TCP ports on this PC:
sudo nmap -p- -T4 192.168.1.8

Scan nearby Wi-Fi networks
sudo iw dev wlan0 scan


For a cleaner list:
sudo iw dev wlan0 scan | grep -E "SSID:|signal:|freq:"
